/target
# Per-worktree CARGO_TARGET_DIR (AGENTS.md "Delegation"). Not covered by `/target`,
# and a `git add -A` inside an agent worktree otherwise stages ~3600 build
# artifacts along with the change.
/target-agent
/.vscode/
*.pb.bin
testing/diffrig/captures/

# Markdown is ignored by default so scratch notes don't accumulate in history.
# Everything below is re-included because it is LOAD-BEARING: each is cited by
# name from tracked source, so a fresh clone without it has dead links.
#
# The planning docs were local-only until 2026-08-01. That stopped being
# tenable once the code started citing them — `git grep` counts ADR-0004 55
# times, ADR-0003 34, internal-docs/envoy-divergences.md 13.
# A `// see ADR-0004` comment pointing at a file nobody else has is worse than
# no comment. They also had no backup: one design doc existed in exactly one
# place, on one laptop, which is the same failure mode as AGENTS.md "Delegation"
# with a different cause.
*.md
!README.md
# The release record. Cited by internal-docs/MILESTONES.md and by the v0.0.1 tag.
!CHANGELOG.md
# The security policy. Needs an entry here for the same reason everything else
# in this list does -- `*.md` denies by default, so a new root-level Markdown
# file is untracked and silent unless allowed. A SECURITY.md that is not in the
# repository is worse than none: it looks present locally and is invisible to
# the people it exists for.
!SECURITY.md
!testing/corpus/fixtures/**/SOURCES.md
# The spec the Go QA suite is written from — reviewable alongside the tests
# that cite its case IDs.
!testing/qa/SCENARIOS.md
# Normative plan, milestone/ship-gate definitions, and architecture decisions.
!internal-docs/**/*.md
!internal-docs/**/*.yaml
!internal-docs/**/*.json
# Implementation contracts cited by the operational telemetry code.
!docs/telemetry-design.md
# The published documentation site. Every page under here is Markdown, so
# `*.md` denied all of them by default and each one had to be `git add -f`'d
# — which means a page an author forgot to force-add was invisible to
# `git status` and simply never shipped. Found 2026-09-08, when a finished
# `operations/running-in-production.md` read as "never written" because the
# only thing `git status` showed was the sidebar entry pointing at it.
!docs/site/**/*.md

admin-ui/node_modules/
admin-ui/dist/

# Browser-automation output: the Playwright/browse bridge drops console logs
# and page snapshots at the repository root whenever a session drives the
# admin UI from here. Tool output, not repo content -- left alone it shows up
# as untracked noise in `git status`, and it reappears as soon as the next
# session starts, so ignoring it beats repeatedly deleting it.
.playwright-mcp/

# Local agent tooling (agent definitions, skills, Claude Code settings).
/.agents/
/.claude/

# Python bytecode from running scripts/*.py (check-deps, check-citations, ...).
__pycache__/

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# Local research output (competitor reports and notes); not tracked.
/internal-docs/reports/
/internal-docs/research_notes/
